---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="How to Check Quilt Pattern Yardage"
  description="Compare pattern-stated yardage with a fresh-fabric plan without confusing stock on hand with the comparison basis."
  eyebrow="Learn QuiltClarity · Pattern comparison"
  guideSlug="check-pattern-yardage"
  guideCategory="start_here"
  previous={{
    href: '/guides/add-fabric-you-have/',
    label: 'Add Fabric You Already Have',
  }}
  next={{
    href: '/guides/read-your-shopping-plan/',
    label: 'Read Your Shopping Plan',
  }}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Compare like with like</h2><p>
      Enter the pattern amount and, when known, the usable WOF it assumes. A
      different current usable width makes the comparison informative but not
      directly like-for-like.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Keep stock out of the comparison</h2><p>
      Pattern yardage describes a fresh purchase scenario. Fabric already owned
      may reduce what you need to buy now, but it must not reduce the fresh
      comparison basis to zero.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>A difference is not an error verdict</h2><p>
      Construction method, trimming, shrinkage, squaring, miscuts, fussy
      cutting, direction, and designer preference can justify allowances. Use
      the <a href="/fabric-cutting-planner/">project planner</a> to see the fresh
      comparison and stock-aware shortfall separately.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
